    "chunk_text": "This beo\u00fe \u00f0a land ymere \u00f0e Wlfrun hafa\u00fe, don into \u00f0a mynstre in Hamtune, & \u00f0e tune nome \u00f0e \u00f0is Erest of Earnleie, & Espich, & Bilsetnatun, & Willenhale, & Wodnesfeld, & Weoleshale, & Ocgintun, & This beo\u00fe \u00f0a mere into Earnleie. Erest of Earesbroce & \u00f0a scorte \u00f0ornes & of \u00f0a scorte \u00f0ornes in Wlsieshorsecroft & \u00f0anen in & of \u00f0e scagan in Eadulfescrofte, & of \u00f0a crofte in \u00f0one ryewei, onlang \u00f0ane riewei in \u00f0a eordbriche, & & of \u00f0a sea\u00fee in Heortseges broc, onlang \u00f0es broces in \u00f0a my\u00fean, & of \u00f0are my\u00feen in Byinnigbroc. & \u00f0anen up efter broce in \u00f0at sych, & of \u00f0an sich in Sciteresford, & of \u00f0an forde in Bromescumbe, & of Onlang Sefernes in fif aken, of fif aken in \u00f0one styb, & of \u00f0a stibbe in \u00f0a strete, onlang strete in winnan Onlang beches in Seferne, up efter Seferne in Leofrichesymere, onlang \u00f0e mere in Thurulfesweie, of \u00f0e & of \u00f0e leie on Earesbroc \u00f0er hit er on feng, & ouer Fatestal into Earnleie et \u00f0ere wich, and \u00f0ritti This beo\u00fe \u00f0e land ymere into Eiswich. Erest of ebles bece in \u00f0a dic, & of \u00f0a dice on Sture dun efter into Tresel, up efter Tresel in & of \u00f0a forde on \u00f0at sic, onlang sices upward in Belstowe, & of Belstowa in Tresel. This beo\u00fe",
